"Adamusan" <adaminnippon@yahoo.com.au> writes:
> I came across a genearl store shopkeeper, with the name "Aklavik", on
> DL2, and also a general store shopkeeper with the same name "Aklavik"
> in minetown!
> Not that it really matters or affects the game in anyway, but just
> wondering if this SHOULD happen?

The randomisation of shopkeeper names is... obscure. The only explicit
constraint is that two shopkeepers on the same _level_ can't have the
same name; otherwise, the choice is determined by a vaguely random
seed and the ID number for the level you're on. It's very observable
that this does _not_ create anything like a flat distribution across
the names available, because of shop-creation's bias towards shallower
levels; you're far more likely to see an Asidonhopo than a Kopasker.

> Do shopkeepers have the same name if they run the same kind of store in
> the same incarnation of the game?

All shopkeepers of a given name will run the same kind of shop, since
the names are chosen from separate lists. The reverse won't happen
very often, but it can (once the ID number for the level gets too big,
a name is just picked completely at random; that'll be what happened
in your Minetown case, since the Mines are numbered after Gehennom).

